      "message": "When the cache is disabled, the `NoAuthTokenCache.get(accountId)` will return an empty list here. This means no access to tokens at all when the cache is disabled?\n\nI think that the setup regarding the cache/no-cache scenarios should rather be at the `AuthTokenAccessor` level:\n* this class shall become an interface\n* `DirectAuthTokenAccessor implements AuthTokenAccessor` shall implement direct (no-cache) access\n* `CachingAuthTokenAccessor implements AuthTokenAccessor` shall wrap a `DirectAuthTokenAccessor` and access it through a guava loading cache.",
